# SRG-APP-000910-AU-000390  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must include only approved trust anchors in trust
# stores or certificate stores managed by the organization.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000910-AU-000390
group:           V-263582
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004909
control_rev5:    SC-17

contribution:    Splunk can be pointed at a single organization-curated PEM trust store,
                 restricted to that store rather than the operating system's anchors, made
                 to validate the certificates it is presented, and made to check
                 certificate revocation status.

governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath non_empty
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] caTrustStore equals splunk
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] certificateStatusValidationMethod equals crl
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] sslVerifyServerCert in 1|true
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslRootCAPath absent
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslRootCAPath https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/outputs.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] caTrustStore https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] certificateStatusValidationMethod https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslVerifyServerCert https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/server.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The content of the trust store file, which the organization populates with
                 approved anchors and which the SPLK-CL-000450 check text verifies with
                 openssl on the host operating system
external:        Operating system file permissions on the trust store and certificate
                 revocation list files
external:        The certificate authority's revocation list distribution, which must be
                 retrieved and placed on the host for crl validation to have data
external:        The organization's determination of which trust anchors are approved

citation:        SRG-APP-000910-AU-000390 check text; SPLK-CL-000450 check and fix text;
                 server.conf.spec:798-824, 902-937, 996-1009, 1125-1145, 5392;
                 outputs.conf.spec:691-699
finding:         Splunk does not restrict certificate validation to the
                 organization-managed trust store: server.conf [sslConfig] sslRootCAPath is
                 unset, caTrustStore admits the operating system anchors, certificate
                 status validation is off, server certificates are not verified, or a
                 deprecated per-output trust store is still configured in outputs.conf.
